WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.280
Almost every equilibrium calculation is one of five

00:00:03.360 --> 00:00:06.880
types: the three from the ICE table videos,

00:00:06.920 --> 00:00:07.680
and two more.

00:00:08.320 --> 00:00:09.920
What you are given, and what you are

00:00:10.080 --> 00:00:11.520
asked, tells you which.

00:00:12.480 --> 00:00:14.640
Settled amounts, and you want K.

00:00:15.120 --> 00:00:17.360
A start plus one settled value.

00:00:17.920 --> 00:00:20.240
K and a start, asking for the settled

00:00:20.320 --> 00:00:21.280
concentrations.

00:00:21.840 --> 00:00:24.320
A mixture and a K, asking which way

00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:25.040
it goes.

00:00:25.520 --> 00:00:28.560
Or an old equilibrium, something added, and a

00:00:28.640 --> 00:00:29.360
new value.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:32.080
We take them in turn, and spend longest

00:00:32.160 --> 00:00:34.240
on the last one, the hardest.

00:00:35.467 --> 00:00:37.826
Type one: settled amounts.

00:00:38.107 --> 00:00:42.106
A two litre vessel holds 0.300 moles of

00:00:42.187 --> 00:00:46.746
sulfur dioxide, 0.150 of oxygen and

00:00:46.867 --> 00:00:50.146
0.600 of sulfur trioxide.

00:00:50.427 --> 00:00:54.666
K uses concentrations, so divide by two first:

00:00:54.747 --> 00:00:59.306
0.150, 0.0750 and

00:00:59.427 --> 00:01:02.506
0.300 moles per litre.

00:01:02.827 --> 00:01:05.706
Write the expression with the coefficients as powers,

00:01:05.787 --> 00:01:10.746
not multipliers, and K is 0.300 squared,

00:01:10.827 --> 00:01:16.746
over the product of 0.150 squared and 0.0750,

00:01:16.827 --> 00:01:18.986
which is 53.3.

00:01:19.067 --> 00:01:22.266
Use moles and you get 26.7, which is

00:01:22.467 --> 00:01:22.826
wrong.

00:01:24.034 --> 00:01:27.793
Type two: a start and one settled value.

00:01:28.114 --> 00:01:32.993
Put 0.400 moles of sulfur dioxide and 0.300

00:01:33.114 --> 00:01:36.673
of oxygen in another two litre vessel, at

00:01:36.754 --> 00:01:39.153
a different temperature, and at equilibrium

00:01:39.794 --> 00:01:43.713
sulfur trioxide is 0.160 moles per litre.

00:01:44.274 --> 00:01:49.393
The start is 0.200 and 0.150 moles

00:01:49.474 --> 00:01:50.313
per litre.

00:01:50.674 --> 00:01:54.273
The measured 0.160 goes in the equilibrium row

00:01:54.434 --> 00:01:59.553
first, so sulfur trioxide's change is plus 0.160.

00:02:00.194 --> 00:02:05.233
Then the coefficients: sulfur dioxide falls 0.160 and

00:02:05.394 --> 00:02:06.993
oxygen falls half of that.

00:02:07.554 --> 00:02:13.953
The equilibrium row is 0.0400 and 0.0700,

00:02:14.034 --> 00:02:16.513
and only that row goes into K, giving

00:02:16.594 --> 00:02:17.953
229.

00:02:19.167 --> 00:02:21.926
Type three: K and a start, and you

00:02:21.967 --> 00:02:23.806
want the settled concentrations.

00:02:24.367 --> 00:02:26.606
You may use the quadratic formula, but an

00:02:26.687 --> 00:02:29.566
HSC question never needs it, so look for

00:02:29.647 --> 00:02:31.966
a perfect square or a tiny K.

00:02:32.767 --> 00:02:34.846
N two O four splits into two N

00:02:34.927 --> 00:02:38.126
O two, K is 4.0 times ten to

00:02:38.207 --> 00:02:42.126
the minus four, and the start is 0.500

00:02:42.367 --> 00:02:44.606
moles per litre of N two O four,

00:02:44.687 --> 00:02:45.966
with no N O two.

00:02:46.527 --> 00:02:47.646
Which shortcut fits?

00:02:48.127 --> 00:02:49.166
Find the N O two.

00:02:49.647 --> 00:02:50.766
Pause here to answer.

00:03:01.167 --> 00:03:02.766
If x of the N two O four

00:03:02.847 --> 00:03:05.566
splits, the N two O four left is

00:03:05.647 --> 00:03:10.126
0.500 minus x and N O two is

00:03:10.207 --> 00:03:13.326
two x, so K is two x all

00:03:13.367 --> 00:03:17.406
squared, over 0.500 minus x.

00:03:17.727 --> 00:03:19.766
The bottom is not a square, so the

00:03:19.807 --> 00:03:21.526
square root will not help.

00:03:21.807 --> 00:03:24.046
But K is tiny next to the start,

00:03:24.127 --> 00:03:28.366
so drop the x: 0.500 minus x is

00:03:28.567 --> 00:03:30.766
about 0.500.

00:03:31.967 --> 00:03:36.046
Four x squared over 0.500 is eight x

00:03:36.087 --> 00:03:39.566
squared, and that equals 4.0 times ten to

00:03:39.647 --> 00:03:41.086
the minus four.

00:03:41.207 --> 00:03:44.126
So x squared is 5.0 times ten to

00:03:44.167 --> 00:03:49.246
the minus five, and x is 0.0071.

00:03:49.287 --> 00:03:51.246
N O two is two x, which is

00:03:51.327 --> 00:03:53.486
0.014.

00:03:53.647 --> 00:03:56.206
Test it: the amount taken off the start,

00:03:56.287 --> 00:04:02.446
0.0071, is 1.4 per cent of 0.500,

00:04:02.567 --> 00:04:05.246
under about 5 per cent, so the shortcut

00:04:05.327 --> 00:04:05.966
holds.

00:04:07.167 --> 00:04:09.726
A huge K is the mirror image.

00:04:10.047 --> 00:04:14.766
Start with sulfur trioxide alone, 0.400 moles per

00:04:14.887 --> 00:04:17.966
litre, where K for sulfur dioxide and oxygen

00:04:18.047 --> 00:04:20.846
making it is 4.0 times ten to the

00:04:20.927 --> 00:04:21.246
ten.

00:04:21.807 --> 00:04:24.846
Almost nothing splits, so let the oxygen be

00:04:25.007 --> 00:04:25.406
x.

00:04:25.887 --> 00:04:29.086
Sulfur dioxide is two x, and sulfur trioxide

00:04:29.167 --> 00:04:31.646
is about 0.400.

00:04:32.867 --> 00:04:38.866
In K, 0.400 squared is 0.160,

00:04:39.027 --> 00:04:44.306
and 0.160 over four x cubed is 0.040

00:04:44.467 --> 00:04:45.986
over x cubed.

00:04:46.107 --> 00:04:48.546
So x cubed is one times ten to

00:04:48.587 --> 00:04:51.746
the minus twelve, and x is one times

00:04:51.827 --> 00:04:53.106
ten to the minus four.

00:04:54.334 --> 00:04:57.213
Test it: the amount taken off the start,

00:04:57.294 --> 00:05:01.933
two x, is 0.00020, a

00:05:02.174 --> 00:05:05.613
tiny part of 0.400.

00:05:05.694 --> 00:05:06.973
Now the other way round.

00:05:07.214 --> 00:05:09.533
If you started with just the reactants, in

00:05:09.574 --> 00:05:11.853
the ratio of the equation, and K was

00:05:12.014 --> 00:05:14.413
huge, nearly all of it would turn to

00:05:14.614 --> 00:05:16.813
products first, and you would take a small

00:05:16.894 --> 00:05:18.493
x back from there.

00:05:18.574 --> 00:05:21.053
An excess of one reactant would stay.

00:05:22.267 --> 00:05:25.466
Type four: a mixture and a K, asked

00:05:25.547 --> 00:05:26.346
for a direction.

00:05:26.907 --> 00:05:30.106
Carbon, a solid in excess, sits with carbon

00:05:30.147 --> 00:05:32.266
dioxide and carbon monoxide.

00:05:32.827 --> 00:05:38.506
K is 1.90, carbon dioxide is 0.500 moles

00:05:38.587 --> 00:05:43.306
per litre and carbon monoxide is 0.800.

00:05:43.387 --> 00:05:45.066
Work out Q for this mixture.

00:05:45.547 --> 00:05:46.586
Which way will it run?

00:05:47.147 --> 00:05:48.426
Pause here to answer.

00:05:58.834 --> 00:06:00.193
Leave the solid out.

00:06:00.474 --> 00:06:06.273
Q is 0.800 squared over 0.500,

00:06:06.354 --> 00:06:09.273
which is 1.28, below K.

00:06:09.554 --> 00:06:12.033
That is too little product, so the forward

00:06:12.114 --> 00:06:15.473
reaction wins and carbon monoxide builds up.

00:06:15.554 --> 00:06:19.113
Q chases K: below it, Q climbs.

00:06:19.394 --> 00:06:23.153
If carbon monoxide were 1.50 moles per litre,

00:06:23.234 --> 00:06:26.473
Q would be 4.50, above K, and it

00:06:26.514 --> 00:06:27.473
would run back.

00:06:28.700 --> 00:06:32.300
Type five is the hardest: an amount added.

00:06:32.620 --> 00:06:35.900
Carbon monoxide and steam make carbon dioxide and

00:06:35.980 --> 00:06:41.180
hydrogen, K is 4.00, and a 2.00 litre

00:06:41.260 --> 00:06:45.820
vessel holds, at equilibrium, 0.400 moles

00:06:45.860 --> 00:06:50.860
of carbon monoxide, 0.400 of steam and 0.800

00:06:50.940 --> 00:06:54.620
each of carbon dioxide and hydrogen.

00:06:54.940 --> 00:06:57.500
Steam is added, and the new equilibrium has

00:06:57.580 --> 00:07:01.060
0.200 moles of carbon monoxide.

00:07:01.340 --> 00:07:02.940
How much steam was added?

00:07:03.260 --> 00:07:07.900
First convert to moles per litre: 0.200,

00:07:07.980 --> 00:07:13.980
0.200, 0.400, 0.400.

00:07:14.020 --> 00:07:17.660
The new carbon monoxide is 0.100.

00:07:18.867 --> 00:07:21.426
Right after the steam goes in, before anything

00:07:21.507 --> 00:07:24.786
reacts, the vessel is the old equilibrium plus

00:07:24.867 --> 00:07:26.386
the extra steam.

00:07:26.467 --> 00:07:28.946
So the unknown goes in the initial row:

00:07:29.027 --> 00:07:33.506
steam is the old 0.200 plus y, where

00:07:33.587 --> 00:07:35.666
y is the added steam in moles per

00:07:35.747 --> 00:07:36.786
litre.

00:07:36.827 --> 00:07:40.866
The new carbon monoxide, 0.100, goes in the

00:07:40.987 --> 00:07:44.626
equilibrium row first, so its change is 0.100

00:07:44.707 --> 00:07:49.426
minus the old 0.200, which is

00:07:49.627 --> 00:07:53.426
minus 0.100, and the ratio is one to

00:07:53.507 --> 00:07:55.026
one all round.

00:07:55.107 --> 00:07:58.946
Steam also falls 0.100, because some of the

00:07:59.067 --> 00:08:01.186
added steam is used up, and the two

00:08:01.267 --> 00:08:04.466
products each rise 0.100.

00:08:05.667 --> 00:08:10.386
At equilibrium that is 0.100, 0.100

00:08:10.507 --> 00:08:15.026
plus y, 0.500 and

00:08:15.147 --> 00:08:17.026
0.500.

00:08:17.347 --> 00:08:19.826
K has not changed, because the temperature has

00:08:19.947 --> 00:08:22.626
not: it is 4.00.

00:08:22.787 --> 00:08:27.746
So 0.500 times 0.500,

00:08:27.867 --> 00:08:32.546
all over 0.100 times the bracket 0.100

00:08:32.627 --> 00:08:37.266
plus y, equals 4.00.

00:08:37.307 --> 00:08:39.826
Solve for y, in moles per litre.

00:08:40.067 --> 00:08:41.506
Pause here and try it.

00:08:51.934 --> 00:08:57.793
The top is 0.250, so 0.100 plus

00:08:57.854 --> 00:09:02.333
y is 0.250 divided by the product of

00:09:02.414 --> 00:09:08.973
4.00 and 0.100, which is 0.625,

00:09:09.054 --> 00:09:13.253
and y is 0.525 moles per litre.

00:09:13.614 --> 00:09:17.213
The vessel is 2.00 litres, so the steam

00:09:17.294 --> 00:09:19.933
added is 1.05 moles.

00:09:20.494 --> 00:09:25.133
Check: 0.250 divided by the product of 0.100

00:09:25.294 --> 00:09:30.813
and 0.625 is 4.00.

00:09:30.894 --> 00:09:34.733
The slips: 0.525 on its own forgets the

00:09:34.814 --> 00:09:35.693
volume.

00:09:35.774 --> 00:09:39.373
0.425 moles per litre forgets that some steam

00:09:39.454 --> 00:09:40.253
was used up.

00:09:41.467 --> 00:09:43.386
Your turn, with a solid.

00:09:43.707 --> 00:09:47.306
Carbon, in excess, reacts with carbon dioxide to

00:09:47.387 --> 00:09:52.266
make carbon monoxide, and K is 0.400 at

00:09:52.347 --> 00:09:53.306
this temperature.

00:09:53.627 --> 00:09:57.466
In a 1.00 litre vessel at equilibrium, carbon

00:09:57.547 --> 00:10:02.346
dioxide and carbon monoxide are each 0.400 moles

00:10:02.427 --> 00:10:02.986
per litre.

00:10:03.627 --> 00:10:06.026
Carbon dioxide is then added, and at the

00:10:06.107 --> 00:10:10.746
new equilibrium carbon monoxide is 0.500 moles

00:10:10.827 --> 00:10:11.666
per litre.

00:10:12.027 --> 00:10:14.666
How many moles of carbon dioxide were added?

00:10:14.907 --> 00:10:16.266
Pause here to answer.

00:10:26.667 --> 00:10:30.986
The new carbon monoxide, 0.500, goes in the

00:10:31.147 --> 00:10:36.506
equilibrium row, so its change is 0.500 minus

00:10:36.587 --> 00:10:41.866
0.400, which is plus 0.100.

00:10:41.907 --> 00:10:44.986
The equation makes two for each carbon dioxide,

00:10:45.067 --> 00:10:49.706
so 0.050 of carbon dioxide was used.

00:10:49.787 --> 00:10:54.426
The new carbon dioxide is 0.500 squared over

00:10:54.507 --> 00:10:58.666
0.400, 0.625.

00:10:58.747 --> 00:11:04.586
That is 0.400 plus y minus 0.050,

00:11:04.707 --> 00:11:08.106
so y is 0.275 moles.

00:11:08.427 --> 00:11:12.186
A 0.225 answer forgot the carbon dioxide used

00:11:12.267 --> 00:11:17.306
up, and 0.325 did not halve the 0.100.

00:11:18.534 --> 00:11:20.373
So read what you are given and what

00:11:20.454 --> 00:11:21.253
you are asked.

00:11:22.214 --> 00:11:26.133
Settled amounts: divide by the volume, find K.

00:11:26.294 --> 00:11:29.773
A start and one value: ICE table, with

00:11:29.814 --> 00:11:32.933
the measured value in the equilibrium row first.

00:11:33.014 --> 00:11:36.613
A start and a K, for concentrations: x,

00:11:36.694 --> 00:11:39.333
then a perfect square, or a tiny or

00:11:39.654 --> 00:11:41.093
huge K, and test any

00:11:41.654 --> 00:11:42.093
shortcut.

00:11:42.134 --> 00:11:44.773
A mixture and a K, for a direction:

00:11:45.094 --> 00:11:45.613
Q.

00:11:45.654 --> 00:11:48.693
An amount added: y in the initial row,

00:11:48.934 --> 00:11:51.613
K unchanged, answer in moles.

00:11:51.814 --> 00:11:53.573
Next: temperature and K.

00:11:54.800 --> 00:11:56.240
Here are the key notes.

00:11:56.480 --> 00:11:58.400
Pause the video if you need more time

00:11:58.480 --> 00:11:59.280
to copy them.
